00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.110 align:start position:0%
way back in 2003 the final matrix film  the matrix revolutions hit the big  screen it's hardly regarded as the  strongest installment in the famed  trilogy and by the time it left theaters  the matrix craze had significantly died  down with the 2020s continuing the trend  of endless reboots and sequels  excitement is back in the air for the  matrix resurrections which will debut  december 2021 and presumably pick up  where revolutions left off there's no  better time to begin refreshing your  memory on everything the matrix  franchise has to offer beginning with  the 1999 film that captivated a  generation from deep allegories that  carry more meaning today to innovative  filmmaking techniques that changed  cinema forever the matrix was by all  accounts a game changer it presented  audiences with philosophical quandaries  in an easy to understand way packed a  punch through its unique action  sequences and told a story that was more  than worth the price of admission plus  it added some incredible characters to  the pop culture pantheon if you're  killed in the matrix  you die here the body cannot live  without the mind  there's no denying keanu reeves neo is  the poster child of the matrix but one  would be remiss not to give carrie and  moss's trinity the spotlight she  deserves she played a big hand in the  first film story cementing her legacy  through one particular scene that still  has fans pausing rewinding and watching  again as we enter the matrix universe  for the first time it's made clear that  something isn't quite right a green  tinted dystopia looks like a normal city  but we feel in our bones that the whole  setup is different from the world that  we know we move to the interior of a  building swarmed by cops eventually  meeting trinity sitting at a computer i  think we can handle one little girl  despite being busted presumably for a  serious crime she refuses to go quietly  and delivers arguably the coolest  looking kick in the history of motion  pictures trinity hovering before a  dumbfounded police officer has become  the defining image of the character even  for those who've never seen the matrix  the scene itself has been parodied to  death over the years most recently  getting an homage in 2021's space jam a  new legacy the reason it's so iconic is  because of its use of a bullet time  camera rig it's a setup that included  dozens of cameras all in operation at  the same time capturing a 360 degree  image that appears frozen combine that  with a green screen carry an moss on  cables and slow motion after effects and  you've got yourself an unforgettable  movie moment when viewers watched  trinity leap into the air for the first  time it was clear that the matrix wasn't  going to look or feel like any action  movie before it the 1999 film is a  showstopper from beginning to end but no  other scene captured that pause-worthy  wow factor like trinity's kick the  famous trinity kick is an excellent  example of how the matrix and its  sequels changed the way hollywood's  general audiences think about visual  effects it was as if the collective  zeitgeist took the red pill and had  their eyes opened to a new way of  filming action sequences the matrix took  the art of the fight scene to a new  level by bringing in one of the biggest  names in the game to choreograph various  sequences the matrix directors lana and  lily wachowski hired director yoon woo  ping to train the actors for six months  prior to filming according to unilad at  the time focusing on stunt choreography  for that long was unheard of for a  hollywood film but the matrix proved  that fight scenes could be more than  punching and kicking with the right  people on board you could create a  visually stunning scene that rivals any  car chase but the matrix did far more  than merely give us cooler set pieces  the sci-fi flake altered the way people  think about not just action in movies  but philosophy the film was able to  seamlessly blend the two without the  matrix we may not have had inception  eternal sunshine of the spotless mind  and district 9 just to name a few and of  course we also wouldn't have the matrix  resurrections which drops in theaters  and on hbo max on december 22nd 2021  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movie scenes are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

